>> title: Goma-Dare
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: sesame, japanese, salad, noodles, no-cook
>> counters: Ramen Shop, The Bowl Shop, Japanese Home Cooking
>> aka: goma dare, gomadare, sesame dressing, sesame sauce
>> servings: 8
>> time: 15 min
>> slack: forgiving — seeds toasted a shade too dark make a bitter paste, and nothing sweetens it back out once it is ground

>> step: grind to a coarse paste
Grind @toasted white sesame seeds{1/2%cup}(70 g) to a coarse, oily paste in a #suribachi{}.

>> step: grind in
Grind @soy sauce{3%Tbs}(45 mL), @mirin{2%Tbs}, and @sugar{2%tsp} into @&(~1)sesame paste{}.

>> step: whisk in
Whisk @rice vinegar{1%Tbs}, @toasted sesame oil{1%tsp}, and @ginger{1%tsp}(grated) into @&(~1)base{}.

>> step: thin to pouring consistency
Thin @&(~1)dressing{} with @dashi{3%Tbs}(45 mL; or water) until it coats a spoon.
